 User wants to find a matrix that corresponds to rotating about the origin by an angle of $45^\circ$ clockwise.
Answer: To find the matrix that corresponds to rotating about the origin by an angle of $45^\circ$ clockwise, we need to calculate the rotation matrix.
<answer> The rotation matrix that corresponds to rotating about the origin by an angle of $45^\circ$ clockwise is

$$R = \begin{bmatrix}
\cos(-45^\circ) & -\sin(-45^\circ) \\
\sin(-45^\circ) & \cos(-45^\circ)
\end{bmatrix} \\ = \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} & \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\
-\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} & \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
\end{bmatrix} \\$$

